+# Feature Specification: Fix SKU lookup, free-shipping threshold and line VAT rounding
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-20 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Reports from sales desk (lower-case SKU refused), a customer (delivery charged at €50.00), accounting (line VAT one cent low).
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Lower-case SKUs are accepted (P1)
+Keying `lb-220` (or ` lb-220 `) orders the same product as `LB-220`.
+**Acceptance**: Given product LB-220, when an order names `lb-220`, then it is placed with SKU shown as `LB-220`; catalogue find/get/reprice/deactivate behave the same.
+
+### User Story 2 - Free shipping at exactly €50.00 (P1)
+**Acceptance**: goods of €50.00 after all discounts → shipping €0 (and no shipping VAT); €49.99 → weight-band cost.
+
+### User Story 3 - VAT per line rounds half up (P1)
+**Acceptance**: one item at €1.99, standard rate → line VAT €0.44 (€1.99 × 22% = 0.4378 € → 43.78 cents → 44).
+
+## Edge Cases
+- README rules affected: Products (SKU case-insensitivity), Shipping (free from €50.00), VAT (half up per line), Money (half up).
+- Boundary: exactly €50.00 goods; €49.99; VAT at exactly 0.5 cent (net 25 cents at 22% = 5.5 → 6; net 125 at 4% = 5.0).
+- Free-shipping threshold looks at goods after coupon and volume discounts.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Catalogue lookups MUST canonicalise SKU (trim, upper-case).
+- **FR-002**: Shipping MUST be free when goods ≥ 5000 cents.
+- **FR-003**: Line VAT MUST be the line net × rate rounded half up to the cent.
+- **FR-004**: Totals MUST remain goods + shipping + VAT + shipping VAT.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All three reported examples produce the expected results; `npm test` passes.
+
+## Assumptions
+- README is authoritative; no README change needed since code was deviating from it.
